ation\">\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"w-Location\">Location</span></h3>\n<p><a href=\"#/wiki/Oramond%20Marshes\">Oramond/Southern Plains</a>, <a href=\"#/wiki/Oramond%20Minotaur%20Camp\">Minotaur Hills</a>, <a href=\"#/wiki/Oramond%20Dungeon\">Oramond Dungeon</a> (depending on Magistrate votes), <a href=\"#/wiki/Underground%20Glooth%20Factory\">Underground Glooth Factory</a>\n</p>\n</div>\n<div id=\"w-creature-behaviour\">\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"w-Behaviour\">Behaviour</span></h3>\n<p>\tA minotaur hunter attacks from a distance. A minotaur hunter will retreat at 56 to 419 (4% - 29.93%, red) health.\n</p>\n</div>\n<div id=\"w-creature-strategy\">\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"w-Strategy\">Strategy</span></h3>\n<p>\tTheir explosion attack is where you'll probably get most damage from. They are usually not a huge threat when they're alone but in groups they quickly become very dangerous. It is suggested to take out any other creatures present before attempting to kill the Minotaur Hunter as they can flee and lure you into an army of other minotaurs. When they haste they are about as fast as a level 160. An energy wall thrown behind their back will block their escape.\n</p>\n</div>\n<div style=\"clear:both;\"></div>\n<div>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"w-Loot\">Loot</span></h3>\n<p><small><i>Drop rates are estimated based on 72,663 samples <span class=\"loot-stats-link\">(Loot Statistics)</span>.</i></small> <small><i>Colour-coding is applied after 500 samples.</i></small><br/><small><i>Task column indicates items used in delivery tasks.</i></small>\n</p>\n<table class=\"wikitable sortable\" style=\"text-align:center; width:auto;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<th></th>\n<th>Item</th>\n<th>Task</th>\n<th>Quantity</th>\n<th>Avg</th>\n<th data-sort-type=\"number\">%\n</th></tr>\n<tr>\n<td><span class=\"loot-table-icon\"><span class=\"no-pseudoelements-container\"><span class=\"mw-default-size\" typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"#/wiki/Gold%20Coin\"><i